  "id": "COMPOUND:22020 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Robinetinidol appears to interact with Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of molecular targets, all of which are involved in the regulation of caspase-5. This interaction is supported by the evidence that Robinetinidol acts as a target for Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Diplotrin A and Lethedioside B. These compounds are likely involved in the same biological pathway, possibly related to cellular stress responses or viral replication. The presence of multiple targets suggests a potential mechanism where Robinetinidol may modulate the activity of these downstream targets, thereby influencing the replication of the replicase polyprotein. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Robinetinidol in regulating viral replication through the Caspase-5 pathway, although the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
